<%- /*
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Lusoris <lusoris@pm.me>
SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2

Caller of the shared required-checks judge, as a consumer keeps it in
.github/workflows/required-checks.yml. Required check: "Required checks".
The forge reports the call as "Required checks / Required checks"; result
reports "Required checks" and fails unless the call passed (decision record
0030, decision record 0108).

Set `required` to the JSON list of every check run and commit-status context
that gates merges in the consumer repository; pass `pull-request-only`,
`not-owed` and `apps` where the consumer has pull-request-scoped checks,
event-excluded checks or non-Actions check producers.

The shared repository, commit and version come from .Shared; the runner
comes from .RunnerTag. The consumer's own licence header comes from .Licence.
Concurrency belongs to the caller, so separate consumers do not collide;
push and merge-group runs key by SHA without cancelling in-progress runs.
*/ -%>
# SPDX-<%/* */%>FileCopyrightText: <% .Licence.CopyrightText %>
# SPDX-<%/* */%>License-Identifier: <% .Licence.Identifier %>
---
# Required checks: wait for and verify every owed check and status on the commit.
# The job is the shared workflow of <% .Shared.Repository %>, named by commit.
name: Required checks

on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review, converted_to_draft]
  push:
    branches: [main]
  merge_group:
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions: {}

concurrency:
  group: required-checks-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.sha }}
  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}

jobs:
  # On a draft the required-checks call is skipped and spends no runner; the
  # result job still takes one runner briefly to report the draft; the check
  # turns red again when a ready pull request is converted to a draft.
  required-checks:
    name: Required checks
    if: >-
      github.event_name != 'pull_request'
      || github.event.pull_request.draft == false
    permissions:
      contents: read # checks out the required-checks judge at its pinned commit
      checks: read # lists check runs on the target commit
      statuses: read # lists commit statuses on the target commit
      actions: read # lists workflow runs on the target commit to exclude foreign events
    uses: <% .Shared.Repository %>/.github/workflows/required-checks.yml@<% .Shared.Commit %> # <% .Shared.Version %>
    with:
      runner: <% .RunnerTag %>
      required: '["Licence", "Secret scan", "Sign-off", "Workflow check"]'

  # The forge reports the calling job above only as
  # "Required checks / Required checks", never as "Required checks", so a rule
  # set that requires "Required checks" waits forever. This job reports
  # "Required checks" and fails unless the call passed; it runs under always()
  # so a failed, cancelled or skipped check still reports here.
  result:
    name: Required checks
    needs: required-checks
    if: always()
    runs-on: <% .RunnerTag %>
    timeout-minutes: 5
    permissions: {}
    steps:
      - name: Report the draft
        if: needs.required-checks.result == 'skipped'
        shell: bash
        run: >
          echo "::error title=Gate not run on a draft::The gate did not run
          because the pull request is a draft.
          It runs when the pull request is marked ready for review."

          exit 1
      - name: Fail unless the required checks passed
        if: needs.required-checks.result != 'success'
        shell: bash
        run: |
          echo "The required checks did not pass or were skipped on a draft."
          exit 1
